__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.agents/
*.egg-info/
internal/
data/
# Claude Code's per-user settings stay out; the project skills under
# .claude/skills/ are routing docs for this repo and ship with it.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
workflows/archive/
# Local symlinks to sister repos checked out elsewhere on the machine. They
# resolve only on the machine that made them, so they are never repo content.
coderef/
update-coderef.sh
# Model weights and tensor dumps are never repo content. This rule lives here
# rather than only in a machine-level ignore config: on 2026-08-28 the 37 MB of
# `bench/results/*.safetensors` on this box were excluded by a global rule
# only, so the repo was protected by one machine's setup and a fresh checkout
# would have committed them. The evidence base is the JSON and JSONL beside
# them, which stay tracked and are small.
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
